1
00:00:00,159 --> 00:00:02,629
(Shedon:)Which leads me to my answer.

2
00:00:02,629 --> 00:00:04,329
(Shedon:)I would choose the ability

3
00:00:04,330 --> 00:00:06,860
(Shedon:)to read people's minds.

4
00:00:06,866 --> 00:00:10,066
(Penny:)Well, I can't read
people's minds.

5
00:00:10,069 --> 00:00:11,569
(Penny:)Actually, that's not true.

6
00:00:11,571 --> 00:00:12,871
(Penny:)I can read men's minds.

7
00:00:12,872 --> 00:00:15,302
(Penny:)But only 'cause it's
usually the one thing.

8
00:00:16,309 --> 00:00:19,779
(Sheldon:)When are we going
to get robot eyes?

9
00:00:19,779 --> 00:00:23,549
(Penny:)You're all alike.

10
00:00:23,549 --> 00:00:25,879
(Sheldon:)Well, what I meant was...

11
00:00:25,885 --> 00:00:28,285
(Sheldon:)I often misinterpret

12
00:00:28,287 --> 00:00:30,017
(Sheldon:)how others are feeling.

13
00:00:30,023 --> 00:00:32,993
(Sheldon:)Like, I can't always tell
if someone is only joking

14
00:00:32,992 --> 00:00:34,922
(Sheldon:)or laughing at me.

15
00:00:34,927 --> 00:00:37,427
(Sheldon:)You know, like, uh, if they're
mad at something I've done

16
00:00:37,430 --> 00:00:39,360
(Sheldon:)or just in a bad mood.

17
00:00:39,365 --> 00:00:41,295
It-it's incredibly stressful.

18
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:44,140
(Penny:)Really? You always
seem so confident.

19
00:00:44,137 --> 00:00:45,437
(Sheldon:)Well, I'm not.

20
00:00:45,438 --> 00:00:47,238
(Sheldon:)And if I could read
people's minds,

21
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:50,440
(Sheldon:)life would be so much simpler.

22
00:00:50,443 --> 00:00:53,413
(Penny:)Well, now I wish I had

23
00:00:53,413 --> 00:00:56,083
(Penny:)the ability to make
that stuff easier for you.

24
00:00:58,351 --> 00:00:59,381
(Sheldon:)Thank you.

